    {
      "id": "shopify-section-template--21565161570358__dossier",
      "classes": "shopify-section",
      "y": 4902.109375,
      "height": 925.171875,
      "text": "TRANSPARENCY\nINTRINSIC VALUE\n\nCraftsmanship is subtraction.\n\nEach piece takes 15 to 20 days. That time goes to the essentials.\n\nWith the illusion of value stripped away, what remains is the piece itself\u2014the leather, the hardware, and the craftsmanship behind it.\n\nDAY 01-03\nLeather Selection & Cutting\n\nTexture often says more than words. Full-grain leather is sourced from tanneries certified Gold by the Leather Working Group (LWG). Heavy surface coatings are avoided, preserving the leather\u2019s natural grain, supple texture, and individual character. Each hide is carefully selected and precisely cut so the panels come together in a balanced, consistent composition.\n\nDAY 04-08\nThread Selection & Stitching\n\nEach well-placed stitch gives the form its strength. Selected to meet exacting standards for texture, strength, flexibility, and finish, the thread gives each seam a clean, precise expression. Carefully controlled spacing and tension support the bag\u2019s structure while refining its overall feel.\n\nDAY 09-13\nEdge Paint & Finishing\n\nRefinement is visible in every edge. Specially selected edge paint creates a fine, subtly textured finish with a light and refined appearance. Built up in multiple thin layers, it gives the edges quiet depth without making them feel heavy. Its flexibility and adhesion allow the finish to sit naturally with the leather, adding definition to the silhouette and detail of the bag.\n\nDAY 14-15+\nFinal Quality Inspection\n\nNothing is finished until every detail is in place. Before packaging, every bag is reviewed for silhouette, panel alignment, stitch consistency, edge finish, leather condition, and hardware function. Only pieces that meet the required standards are approved for release.",
      "headings": [
        {
          "tag": "H2",
